 R←Test_002(debugFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ns;r
⍝ `Notify` must never bring an application down, because `CommTools` does not trap errors in
⍝ the notifier. Fixed into a namespace without a `TatinVars` it cannot find `toast.ps1`, and
⍝ that failure must be swallowed, recorded in `∆NotifyError` and reported as `⍬`.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 ns←⎕NS''                                       ⍝ No `TatinVars` in here
 {}ns.⎕FX ##.WindowsToast.⎕NR'Notify'

 :Trap 0   ⍝ Nothing at all may escape from `Notify`, so this catches everything
     r←ns.Notify'YesOrNo' 'Test_002: nobody should ever see this'
 :Else
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1                            ⍝ An error escaped after all
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp ⍬≢r
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=ns.⎕NC'∆NotifyError'           ⍝ The error must have been kept for diagnosis
 →T.GoToTidyUp 6≠ns.∆NotifyError.EN             ⍝ VALUE ERROR, because `TatinVars` is missing

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
⍝Done
